.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-landed-abandoned 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-landed\-abandoned \- Refuse an In Progress claim with no landing, no pull request, no branch and no recent touch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten landed abandoned\fR [\fB\-\-claimed\fR] [\fB\-\-merged\-prs\fR] [\fB\-\-landed\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-refs\fR] [\fB\-\-instant\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-idle\-days\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Refuse an In Progress claim with no landing, no pull request, no branch and no recent touch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-claimed\fR \fI<claimed>\fR
`<CLOUD\-id>` lines a commit on origin/main closes, from `claimed\-keys \-\-closing\-only`
.TP
\fB\-\-merged\-prs\fR \fI<merged_prs>\fR
`<CLOUD\-id><TAB><pr\-number>` lines, one per closing key in a MERGED pull request
.TP
\fB\-\-landed\-by\fR \fI<landed_by>\fR
`<CLOUD\-id><TAB><ref>` lines the caller asserts carry the work
.TP
\fB\-\-refs\fR \fI<refs>\fR
Branch names the remote carries, one per line
.TP
\fB\-\-instant\fR \fI<instant>\fR
The instant to measure the idle bound against, ISO\-8601 (default: now)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-idle\-days\fR \fI<max_idle_days>\fR
Days a claim may be idle before it reads as abandoned (default: 2)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
